# API Standards

- Preserve documented `/api/*` contracts during migration; use additive changes by default.
- Authenticate with shared Better Auth helpers and authorize role, membership, ownership,
  and account status at every protected object boundary.
- Validate body, path, and query input; bound pagination and collection sizes.
- Return the established resource envelope and documented status/error shape.
- Do not add unsupported CRUD verbs merely for symmetry.
- Map domain errors centrally; do not expose stacks, provider internals, secrets, or PII.
- Apply rate limits to abuse-sensitive and provider-billed routes.
- Add idempotency protection before retryable side effects such as payments and fan-out.
- Document cache/revalidation behavior and avoid user-specific caching leaks.
- Add route integration tests for success, validation, authentication, authorization,
  conflict, provider failure, and backward compatibility.
